# Example 14 — NLopt MLSL_LDS + LN_BOBYQA (single-call global+local).
#
# Multi-Level Single-Linkage with Low-Discrepancy Sampling. MLSL is
# itself a global+local hybrid: it samples the box on an LDS sequence
# and launches a local descent from each sample point — but it skips
# starts that fall in the basin of an already-found minimum. The
# result is K distinct local minima within a controlled budget, with
# no repeat work on the same basin.
#
# Unlike a PRESTAGE strategy, MLSL is one call: the algorithm decides
# itself when to spawn a new sample versus when to refine.
#
# REQUIRED: an INNER block specifying the inner local algorithm. We use
# `LN_BOBYQA` (derivative-free trust-region) so noisy LAMMPS objectives
# don't trip finite-difference gradients.

OPTIMIZER
  INIT
    SEED 1717
  ENDINIT
  STRATEGY
    TYPE PLAIN
    LIB NLOPT
    ALGO G_MLSL_LDS
    MAXEVAL 24
    POPULATION 4
    INNER
      LIB NLOPT
      ALGO LN_BOBYQA
    ENDINNER
  ENDSTRATEGY
ENDOPTIMIZER

LOSS L2
FAILSCORE 1e16
PC_ERMSE 0 0.0001
PC_LAMMPS --script ../common/lammps/Ecoh.in --varloss Ecoh 8.10 800

OPTIM RCUT2B (1) 4.0 6.0
OPTIM SGRIDMB (1) 0.1 0.4

OUTPUT 1
BOUTPUT 1
